# Week 15 – generosity & words
x(P,"Give water, get water",H,"Ever notice that generous people seem lighter?\n\n\"{q}\"\n— Proverbs 11:25\n\nGenerosity is not losing something. It's joining the flow.\n\nWho could use a cup of water from you today?",[("The generous soul will be richly filled. Whoever gives others water will get water himself.","Sprueche:11:25")],"a gold water jug pouring into a cup, the cup overflowing back into the jug"),
x(S,"Abraham on the mountain",ST,["1/ An old man, a long walk, a question from his son he could not answer.\n\nAbraham and Isaac in 60 seconds 🧵","2/ God had promised Abraham a family as many as the stars. Then came a test that made no sense. Abraham walked up the mountain anyway, with a heavy heart.","3/ Isaac asked where the lamb was. His father answered:\n\n\"{q}\"\n— Genesis 22:8","4/ And God did provide. Isaac was safe.\n\nSometimes trust is just this: walking on together, one step at a time, before you see the answer."],[("God himself will provide the lamb for the burnt offering, my son.","1-Mose:22:8")],"an old man and a boy walking up a mountain path at dawn, a ram's silhouette in a thicket at the top"),
x(M,"Faith, simply defined",MW,"What is faith? The Bible's own definition:\n\n\"{q}\"\n— Hebrews 11:1\n\nFaith isn't pretending. It's leaning your weight on what you can't see yet, like sitting down on a chair you trust.",[("Faith is assurance of things hoped for, proof of things not seen.","Hebraeer:11:1")],"a simple chair glowing in gold light on a dark path, a small figure about to sit"),
x(J,"Blessed are those who mourn",H,"If you're grieving right now, this is for you:\n\n\"{q}\"\n— Matthew 5:4\n\nJesus didn't say ‘get over it.’ He said comfort is coming.\n\nTears are not a lack of faith.",[("Blessed are those who mourn, for they will be comforted.","Matthaeus:5:4")],None),
x(MT,"Myth: God loves you once you're good",MV,"Myth: God will love you once you clean up your life.\n\nTruth:\n\"{q}\"\n— Romans 5:8\n\nWhile. Not after. He loved you before you got it together.",[("Christ died for us while we were still sinners.","Roemer:5:8")],"a lantern of gold light held out toward a figure still walking in the dark"),
x(Q,"The best advice you ever got",QQ,"What's the best piece of life advice anyone ever gave you?\n\nOne sentence. Let's build a wall of wisdom 👇",[],None),
x(R,"The Lord is my light",RC,"Sunday. Read this slowly:\n\n\"{q}\"\n— Psalm 27:1\n\nFear shrinks when the light gets bigger.\n\nIf you want the whole Bible in words this clear, with a short explanation for every passage: link in bio.",[("The LORD is my light and my salvation. Whom should I fear?","Psalmen:27:1")],"a single gold lamp shining on a dark path, the shadows retreating"),
# Week 16 – words that heal
x(P,"Words that stab, words that heal",H,"You remember a sentence someone said to you 10 years ago. So does everyone else.\n\n\"{q}\"\n— Proverbs 12:18\n\nPause for 3 seconds before you reply today. It's enough.",[("Some people speak without thinking, and it is like the stabbing of a sword, but the tongue of the wise heals.","Sprueche:12:18")],"a sword turning into a bandage of gold light"),
x(S,"Jacob's ladder",ST,["1/ He cheated his brother, ran away from home, and slept on a rock with a stone for a pillow.\n\nJacob's dream in 60 seconds 🧵","2/ Alone in the dark, Jacob dreamed of a stairway reaching to heaven, with angels going up and down.","3/ And God, of all things, made him a promise:\n\n\"{q}\"\n— Genesis 28:15","4/ God met Jacob at his lowest, not his best.\n\nYour rock-pillow night may be the place God speaks the clearest."],[("Look! I am with you. I will protect you wherever you go.","1-Mose:28:15")],"a stairway of gold light rising from a stone into a starry sky"),
x(M,"What does God actually want?",MW,"People argue about rules. The prophet Micah sums it up in one line:\n\n\"{q}\"\n— Micah 6:8\n\nBe fair. Be kind. Stay humble.\n\nThree things. A whole life.",[("to act justly, to love mercy, and to walk humbly with your God.","Micha:6:8")],"three gold stepping stones on a path labeled with small icons: scales, heart, footprints"),
x(J,"Peacemakers",H,"Being right is easy. Making peace is hard.\n\n\"{q}\"\n— Matthew 5:9\n\nNot peacekeepers who avoid conflict. Peacemakers who walk into it to heal it.",[("Blessed are those who make peace, for they will be called children of God.","Matthaeus:5:9")],"two hands reaching across a broken bridge, gold light filling the gap"),
x(MT,"Myth: Christians are always happy",MVT,["1/ Myth: If you have faith, you should always be happy.\n\nTruth: The apostle Paul, who wrote half the New Testament, describes his life like this 🧵","2/ \"{q}\"\n— 2 Corinthians 4:8–9","3/ Pressed. Puzzled. Hunted. Struck down.\n\nThat's not a fake smile. That's honest pain.","4/ But look at the second half of each line: not crushed, not in despair, not abandoned, not destroyed.\n\nFaith doesn't remove the pressure. It keeps you from breaking."],[("We are pressed on every side, yet not crushed. We are puzzled, yet not in despair. We are hunted, yet not abandoned. We are struck down, yet not destroyed.","2-Korinther:4:8-9")],"a clay jar with cracks, gold light shining through the cracks"),
x(Q,"Words you still remember",QQ,"What's one kind sentence someone said to you that you still remember years later? 👇",[],None),
x(R,"When worries pile up",RC,"For the overthinkers at 2 a.m.:\n\n\"{q}\"\n— Psalm 94:19\n\nWorry is loud. Comfort is quiet. Both are there. Choose which one you listen to.\n\nThe Bible in plain words, all four volumes: link in bio.",[("When there were many worried thoughts inside me, your comfort made my soul glad.","Psalmen:94:19")],"a bedroom window at night, swirling dark thoughts outside, a warm gold glow inside"),
# Week 17 – advice & calling
x(P,"Ask for advice",H,"Going it alone feels strong. It's usually just lonely.\n\n\"{q}\"\n— Proverbs 15:22\n\nWho's one wise person you could ask this week?",[("Where there is no advice, plans fail, but where there are many advisers, they succeed.","Sprueche:15:22")],"a round table with several gold chairs around a glowing map"),
x(S,"Moses and the burning bush",ST,["1/ He was 80, a shepherd in the desert, a man with a failed past. Then a bush caught fire and didn't burn up 🧵","2/ Moses walked closer to look. God spoke:\n\n\"{q}\"\n— Exodus 3:5","3/ God called him to free his people from Egypt. Moses had excuses: I'm nobody. I can't speak well. Send someone else.","4/ God didn't argue with the excuses. He said, I will be with you.\n\nThe ordinary ground you're standing on today might be holy ground."],[("Take off your sandals. For the place where you are standing is holy ground.","2-Mose:3:5")],"a desert bush burning with gold flames that do not consume it, a pair of sandals in the sand"),
x(M,"Light in the darkness",MW,"Feeling like the dark is winning? Read this:\n\n\"{q}\"\n— John 1:5\n\nNot ‘the darkness is gone.’ The darkness hasn't overcome it.\n\nOne candle still wins against a whole dark room.",[("The light shines in the darkness. And the darkness hasn’t overcome it.","Johannes:1:5")],"one small candle flame in a vast dark room, its light reaching every corner"),
x(J,"Love your enemies",H,"The hardest sentence Jesus ever said:\n\n\"{q}\"\n— Matthew 5:44\n\nYou don't have to like them. Start with one prayer. It changes you before it changes them.",[("Love your enemies. Bless those who curse you.","Matthaeus:5:44")],None),
x(MT,"Myth: Prayer must sound holy",MV,"Myth: Prayer needs beautiful words.\n\nTruth: One of the prayers Jesus praised was seven words long:\n\n\"{q}\"\n— Luke 18:13\n\nHonest beats fancy. Every time.",[("God, have mercy on me, a sinner!","Lukas:18:13")],None),
x(Q,"If you could ask for one thing",QQ,"King Solomon could ask God for anything. He asked for wisdom.\n\nIf you could ask for one quality, not a thing, what would it be? 👇",[],None),
x(R,"Healer of broken hearts",RC,"If your heart got broken this year:\n\n\"{q}\"\n— Psalm 147:3\n\nGod doesn't just look at wounds. He bandages them.\n\nEvery psalm, explained in simple words: link in bio.",[("He heals those whose hearts are broken, and he bandages their wounds.","Psalmen:147:3")],"a cracked heart wrapped gently in a ribbon of gold light"),
# Week 18 – self-control
x(P,"Stronger than a hero",H,"Real strength isn't loud.\n\n\"{q}\"\n— Proverbs 16:32\n\nAnyone can lose it. Few can hold it. Be one of the few today.",[("Whoever is slow to anger is better than a mighty hero, and whoever controls himself is better than someone who captures a city.","Sprueche:16:32")],"a calm figure standing still while a city of noise swirls around, gold line art"),
x(S,"Joshua and the walls of Jericho",ST,["1/ A city with massive walls. An army with no siege machines. And the strangest battle plan in history 🧵","2/ God told them: walk around the city. Once a day for six days. Seven times on the seventh day. Say nothing. Just walk.","3/ It looked ridiculous. They did it anyway.\n\n\"{q}\"\n— Joshua 6:20","4/ Some walls don't fall because you push harder. They fall because you keep showing up and obey when it looks foolish."],[("the people shouted with a great shout. Then the wall fell down flat.","Josua:6:20")],"massive city walls crumbling under rays of gold light, trumpets in silhouette"),
x(M,"Nothing can separate you",MW,"The strongest promise in the Bible?\n\n\"{q}\"\n— Romans 8:38–39\n\nNot your past. Not your future. Not your worst day.",[("nothing now and nothing in the future, no powers, nothing high and nothing deep, and nothing else in all creation will be able to separate us from God’s love","Roemer:8:38-39")],"a small figure wrapped in an unbreakable circle of gold light amid storms"),
x(J,"Where your treasure is",H,"Want to know what you really love? Check your calendar and your bank app.\n\n\"{q}\"\n— Matthew 6:21\n\nYour heart follows what you invest in.",[("For where your treasure is, there your heart will be also.","Matthaeus:6:21")],"a treasure chest with a glowing gold heart inside"),
x(MT,"Myth: Anger is always a sin",MV,"Myth: Good people never get angry.\n\nTruth:\n\"{q}\"\n— Ephesians 4:26\n\nAnger is a signal, not a sin. What you do with it is the question. And don't take it to bed.",[("“Be angry, and don’t sin.” Don’t let the sun go down on your anger.","Epheser:4:26")],"a sun setting over a calm sea, the last red clouds fading to gold"),
x(Q,"How do you cool down?",QQ,"When you feel anger rising, what actually helps you cool down?\n\nWalk? Music? Silence? Prayer? 👇",[],None),
x(R,"Find your joy",RC,"Sunday thought:\n\n\"{q}\"\n— Psalm 37:4\n\nWhen God becomes your joy, your wants slowly change, and they become wants worth having.\n\nThe Bible in leichter Sprache, now in English too. Link in bio.",[("Also find your joy in the LORD, and he will give you what your heart wants.","Psalmen:37:4")],"a field of gold wildflowers under a soft morning sun"),
# Week 19 – joy & laughter
x(P,"Laughter is medicine",H,"Science keeps confirming what an old proverb said:\n\n\"{q}\"\n— Proverbs 17:22\n\nWatch something funny. Call the friend who makes you laugh. It counts as self-care.",[("A cheerful heart is good medicine, but a crushed spirit dries up the bones.","Sprueche:17:22")],"a small gold medicine bottle with a smiling sun on the label"),
x(S,"Samuel: Speak, I'm listening",ST,["1/ A boy sleeping in the temple hears his name in the night. Three times he runs to the old priest Eli. Three times Eli says: I didn't call you 🧵","2/ Then Eli understands. It's God calling. He tells the boy what to answer.","3/ \"{q}\"\n— 1 Samuel 3:10","4/ Most of us pray: Listen, Lord, your servant is speaking.\n\nTry the other way today. Five quiet minutes. Just listen."],[("Speak, for your servant is listening.","1-Samuel:3:10")],"a small oil lamp beside a sleeping mat in a dark temple, soft gold glow"),
x(M,"The fruit of the Spirit",MW,"The Bible's list of what a changed life looks like:\n\n\"{q}\"\n— Galatians 5:22–23\n\nFruit, not a to-do list. It grows slowly.\n\nWhich one is growing in you?",[("the fruit of the Spirit is love, joy, peace, patience, kindness, goodness, faith, gentleness and self-control.","Galater:5:22-23")],"a tree with nine glowing gold fruits"),
x(J,"Look at the birds",H,"Anxious?\n\n\"{q}\"\n— Matthew 6:26\n\nWatch a bird for one minute today. You're worth more.",[("Look at the birds of the sky: They don’t sow, they don’t reap, and they don’t gather into barns, yet your heavenly Father feeds them.","Matthaeus:6:26")],"a small bird perched on a branch, gold line art, sunrise"),
x(MT,"Myth: You're too far gone",MVT,["1/ Myth: Some people are too far gone for God.\n\nTruth: Jesus was criticized for eating with exactly those people 🧵","2/ The religious leaders were shocked. Tax collectors? Sinners? At the same table?","3/ Jesus answered:\n\n\"{q}\"\n— Mark 2:17","4/ A hospital is for sick people. A doctor is not disgusted by illness.\n\nIf you feel too broken, you're exactly who he came for."],[("Those who are healthy don’t need a doctor, but those who are sick do.","Markus:2:17")],"a long wooden table with many plates and one warm gold light at its center"),
x(Q,"What made you laugh this week?",QQ,"What made you genuinely laugh this week?\n\nLet's spread some good medicine 👇",[],None),
x(R,"Shelter in the shadow",RC,"Sunday. Rest here a moment:\n\n\"{q}\"\n— Psalm 91:1\n\nYou don't have to be the fortress. You're allowed to hide in one.\n\nPsalms and the whole Bible, explained simply: link in bio.",[("Whoever lives in the secret place of the Most High will rest in the shadow of the Almighty.","Psalmen:91:1-2")],"a small bird resting under a large sheltering wing of gold light"),
# Week 20 – plans and humility
x(P,"Your plans, his plan",H,"Your five-year plan is fine. Just hold it loosely.\n\n\"{q}\"\n— Proverbs 19:21\n\nWhen plans fall apart, it's not always the end. Sometimes it's a redirect.",[("There are many plans in a person’s heart, but the LORD’s plan will stand.","Sprueche:19:21")],"a paper map with one path crossed out and a new gold path drawn in"),
x(S,"Solomon asks for wisdom",ST,["1/ A young king. God appears in a dream and says: Ask for whatever you want 🧵","2/ Money? Long life? Victory over enemies? Solomon asked for none of these.","3/ \"{q}\"\n— 1 Kings 3:9","4/ God was pleased and gave him wisdom, and much more.\n\nWhen you don't know what to pray for, pray for an understanding heart. It's never the wrong request."],[("So give your servant an understanding heart","1-Koenige:3:9")],"a young king kneeling in prayer, a crown set aside, a gold glow above"),
x(M,"Something new is coming",MW,"Stuck in a season that feels like a desert?\n\n\"{q}\"\n— Isaiah 43:19\n\nGod's specialty: roads where there are none. Water where nothing grows.",[("Look, I am doing a new thing. Now it springs up. Don’t you see it? I will make a way in the wilderness and rivers in the desert.","Jesaja:43:19")],"a gold river winding through a dry desert, small green shoots along its banks"),
x(J,"The speck and the beam",H,"Jesus had a sense of humor:\n\n\"{q}\"\n— Matthew 7:3\n\nPicture someone with a wooden beam in their eye trying to remove your eyelash.\n\nCheck your own eye first.",[("Why do you see the speck in your brother’s eye, but don’t notice the beam in your own eye?","Matthaeus:7:3")],None),
x(MT,"Myth: Faith is just a feeling",MV,"Myth: Faith is a warm feeling inside.\n\nTruth:\n\"{q}\"\n— James 2:17\n\nFaith you never act on is like a recipe you never cook.\n\nWhat's one thing you could do today because you believe?",[("faith, if it has no deeds, is dead in itself.","Jakobus:2:17")],None),
x(Q,"A plan that changed for the better",QQ,"Tell us about a plan that fell apart, and something better came instead 👇",[],None),
x(R,"God will teach you the way",RC,"Don't know which way to go?\n\n\"{q}\"\n— Psalm 32:8\n\nYou're not wandering unseen.\n\nIf you want to read the Bible without getting lost in old language: link in bio.",[("I will teach you and show you the way you should go. I will give you advice, and my eye is on you.","Psalmen:32:8")],"a crossroads at dusk with one path softly lit in gold"),
# Week 21 – silence and gossip
x(P,"Starve the fire",H,"Want a fight to end? Stop adding wood.\n\n\"{q}\"\n— Proverbs 26:20\n\nThe next time someone shares gossip, let it end with you.",[("When there is no wood, the fire goes out. Without gossip, a quarrel dies down.","Sprueche:26:20")],"a small campfire going out, the last embers glowing gold, no wood left beside it"),
x(S,"Three men in the fire",ST,["1/ Bow to the golden statue or be thrown into a furnace. Three young men said no 🧵","2/ King Nebuchadnezzar gave them one last chance. Their answer is one of the bravest lines ever written:","3/ \"{q}\"\n— Daniel 3:17–18","4/ ‘But if not.’ That's real faith: trusting God can rescue you, and staying faithful even if he doesn't do it your way.\n\nThey walked out of the fire unharmed."],[("our God whom we serve is able to rescue us from the burning, fiery furnace. And he will rescue us from your hand, O king. But if not, you should know, O king, that we will not serve your gods","Daniel:3:17-18")],"three figures standing calm inside gold flames, a fourth figure of light beside them"),
x(M,"A time for everything",MW,"If life feels out of rhythm:\n\n\"{q}\"\n— Ecclesiastes 3:1\n\nA season of waiting is not wasted. A season of grief is not forever.\n\nWhat season are you in?",[("Everything has its season. There is a time for everything that happens under heaven:","Prediger:3:1")],"a tree shown in four quarters: spring, summer, autumn, winter, in gold line art"),
x(J,"Build on the rock",H,"Everyone's house looks fine on a sunny day.\n\n\"{q}\"\n— Matthew 7:24\n\nThe storm doesn't decide if you stand. The foundation does. Build it before the rain.",[("everyone who hears these words of mine and does them is like a wise man who built his house on the rock.","Matthaeus:7:24")],"a small house on solid rock while storm waves crash below"),
x(MT,"Myth: Temptation means you're bad",MV,"Myth: If you feel tempted, something is wrong with you.\n\nTruth:\n\"{q}\"\n— 1 Corinthians 10:13\n\nEveryone faces it. And there is always a door out. Look for the door.",[("No temptation has come to you except what is common to all people. God is faithful.","1-Korinther:10:13")],"a dark room with one door outlined in gold light"),
x(Q,"Your foundation",QQ,"When everything shakes, what's the one thing that keeps you standing? 👇",[],None),
x(R,"Strength of my heart",RC,"For the tired body and the tired heart:\n\n\"{q}\"\n— Psalm 73:26\n\nYou don't have to be strong. You have a strength outside of you.\n\nRead the whole Bible in clear words: link in bio.",[("My body and my heart fail, but God is the strength of my heart, and he is my share forever.","Psalmen:73:26")],"a weary traveler leaning on a tall staff of gold light"),
# Week 22 – the right word
x(P,"Apples of gold",H,"The right word at the right time is priceless.\n\n\"{q}\"\n— Proverbs 25:11\n\nSomeone today needs to hear ‘I'm proud of you.’ Be the one who says it.",[("A word spoken at the right time is like apples of gold in settings of silver.","Sprueche:25:11")],"golden apples in a delicate silver filigree bowl"),
x(S,"Water into wine",ST,["1/ A wedding. The wine runs out. In that culture, a huge embarrassment for the family 🧵","2/ Jesus' mother noticed. Jesus told the servants to fill six huge stone jars with water and take some to the man in charge.","3/ \"{q}\"\n— John 2:9","4/ His first miracle wasn't in a temple. It was at a party, to save a family from shame.\n\nGod cares about the ordinary moments too."],[("The man in charge of the feast tasted the water. It had now become wine.","Johannes:2:9")],"six stone jars, one with wine glowing deep red and gold"),
x(M,"Perfect peace",MW,"Perfect peace sounds impossible. Here's how Isaiah describes it:\n\n\"{q}\"\n— Isaiah 26:3\n\nPeace isn't the absence of problems. It's a mind anchored somewhere steady.",[("You will keep in perfect peace the one whose mind is steady, because he trusts in you.","Jesaja:26:3")],"a boat anchored in rough water, the anchor line glowing gold"),
x(J,"Every hair counted",H,"Feel invisible?\n\n\"{q}\"\n— Luke 12:7\n\nGod knows you in more detail than you know yourself.",[("God has even counted every hair on your head. So don’t be afraid. You are worth more than many sparrows.","Lukas:12:7")],"a sparrow resting in an open palm of gold light"),
x(MT,"Myth: Giving makes you poorer",MVT,["1/ Myth: The more you give, the less you have.\n\nTruth: Jesus taught the opposite 🧵","2/ \"{q0}\"\n— Luke 6:38","3/ Paul quoted a saying of Jesus that isn't in the Gospels:\n\n\"{q1}\"\n— Acts 20:35","4/ Generous people are not always richer in money. But they are richer in joy, friends and peace.\n\nGive one small thing today and see."],[("Give, and it will be given to you.","Lukas:6:38"),("It is more blessed to give than to receive.","Apostelgeschichte:20:35")],"two open hands, one giving a gold coin, both glowing brighter"),
x(Q,"Who encouraged you?",QQ,"Tag or name someone whose words once kept you going 👇",[],None),
x(R,"Through his gates with thanks",RC,"Sunday gratitude:\n\n\"{q}\"\n— Psalm 100:4\n\nName three things before you check your phone today.\n\nThe Bible, made simple, for anyone who wants to finally understand it: link in bio.",[("Go through his gates with thanks, and into his courtyards with praise!","Psalmen:100:4")],"tall open gates glowing gold at sunrise"),
# Week 23 – humility
x(P,"Watch your mouth",H,"Half of life's trouble starts with one sentence.\n\n\"{q}\"\n— Proverbs 21:23\n\nNot every thought needs to be spoken. Not every comment needs to be posted.",[("Whoever guards his mouth and his tongue keeps his life safe from troubles.","Sprueche:21:23")],None),
x(S,"Peter's empty nets",ST,["1/ A professional fisherman. A whole night of work. Zero fish 🧵","2/ In the morning a carpenter tells him to go back out and throw the nets again. Peter's answer:","3/ \"{q}\"\n— Luke 5:5","4/ The nets filled so full they began to tear.\n\nTired and empty is often right where the miracle begins. Try once more."],[("Master, we worked hard all night and caught nothing. But because you say so, I will let down the nets.","Lukas:5:5")],"a fishing boat at dawn with nets bursting with silver-gold fish"),
x(M,"God's thoughts are higher",MW,"When life makes no sense:\n\n\"{q}\"\n— Isaiah 55:9\n\nYou don't need to understand everything to trust the one who does.",[("as the heavens are higher than the earth, so are my ways higher than your ways and my thoughts than your thoughts.","Jesaja:55:8-9")],"a vast night sky over a tiny figure on a hill, gold stars"),
x(J,"Come away and rest",H,"Jesus once saw his friends so busy they couldn't eat. He said:\n\n\"{q}\"\n— Mark 6:31\n\nRest isn't a reward for finishing everything. It's part of the plan.",[("Come away to a deserted place and rest a while.","Markus:6:31")],"a quiet lakeshore with an empty boat and a small campfire"),
x(MT,"Myth: Rest is lazy",MV,"Myth: Busy = faithful.\n\nTruth:\n\"{q}\"\n— Isaiah 30:15\n\nSometimes the strongest thing you can do is stop and be quiet.",[("Your strength will be in quietness and confidence.","Jesaja:30:15")],None),
