# Week 24 – confession
x(P,"Hiding vs. confessing",H,"Secrets get heavier every day you carry them.\n\n\"{q}\"\n— Proverbs 28:13\n\nSaying ‘I was wrong’ feels like losing. It's actually how you get free.",[("Whoever hides his sins will not succeed, but whoever confesses them and gives them up finds mercy.","Sprueche:28:13")],"a heavy backpack set down on the ground, the figure walking on lighter, gold dawn"),
x(S,"The blind man who saw",ST,["1/ A man blind from birth is healed by Jesus. You'd think everyone would celebrate. Instead, the religious leaders interrogate him 🧵","2/ Who did this? Is he a sinner? How exactly did it happen? They questioned him again and again.","3/ He didn't have all the theological answers. He just said:\n\n\"{q}\"\n— John 9:25","4/ You don't need to win every debate. Your story of what God did for you is enough."],[("I know one thing: I was blind, but now I can see.","Johannes:9:25")],"a pair of eyes opening to a burst of gold sunlight"),
x(M,"Count it all joy?",MW,"Joy when things go wrong? Really?\n\n\"{q}\"\n— James 1:2–3\n\nNot joy because of the pain. Joy because of what the pain is building in you.",[("When your faith is tested, it produces endurance.","Jakobus:1:2-3")],None),
x(J,"Don't judge",H,"Jesus on judging others:\n\n\"{q}\"\n— Luke 6:37\n\nThe freedom you give others comes back to you.",[("Don’t judge, and you won’t be judged. Don’t condemn, and you won’t be condemned. Set others free, and you will be set free.","Lukas:6:37")],"a gold birdcage door opening, a bird flying out"),
x(MT,"Myth: One mistake disqualifies you",MV,"Myth: Mess up badly and God is done with you.\n\nTruth:\n\"{q}\"\n— 1 John 1:9\n\nConfession isn't a punishment. It's a fresh start.",[("If we confess our sins, he is faithful and righteous. He forgives us our sins","1-Johannes:1:9")],None),
