# Week 25 – work & diligence
x(P,"Learn from the ant",H,"No boss. No alarm. No motivation video. Yet the ant gets it done.\n\n\"{q}\"\n— Proverbs 6:6\n\nSmall, steady, daily. That's the whole secret.",[("Go to the ant, you lazy person! Look at her ways, and become wise!","Sprueche:6:6")],"a tiny ant carrying a gold seed up a stem"),
x(S,"Paul and Silas sing in prison",ST,["1/ Beaten. Thrown into the inner cell. Feet locked in wooden stocks 🧵","2/ What would you do at midnight in that place? Complain? Cry? Here's what they did:","3/ \"{q}\"\n— Acts 16:25","4/ An earthquake shook the prison open, and the jailer and his family came to faith that night.\n\nPraise in the dark is never wasted. Someone is always listening."],[("About midnight Paul and Silas were praying and singing hymns to God. The other prisoners were listening to them.","Apostelgeschichte:16:25")],"a dark prison cell with musical notes of gold light floating up through the bars"),
x(M,"Tree by the water",MW,"How to stay green in a dry year:\n\n\"{q}\"\n— Jeremiah 17:8\n\nDrought comes to everyone. Roots decide who stays green.",[("he will be like a tree planted by the water, that spreads out its roots by the stream. It will not be afraid when heat comes.","Jeremia:17:7-8")],"a green tree by a stream with gold roots reaching into the water, dry land around"),
x(J,"I am the vine",H,"Burned out from trying to do it all yourself?\n\n\"{q}\"\n— John 15:5\n\nBranches don't strain to grow fruit. They just stay connected.",[("I am the vine. You are the branches. If you remain in me and I remain in you, you will bear much fruit.","Johannes:15:5")],"a grapevine with gold branches heavy with fruit"),
